# Folder metadata written by cloud-sync clients — Google Drive Desktop in this case, which puts one in
# every folder it manages (the content names `GoogleDriveFS.exe`). `OneDrive litter` was this line's
# earlier description and named the wrong program.
#
# **Ignoring them here is not enough, and that is the trap.** Gradle's resource merger scans the
# filesystem rather than git, so a `desktop.ini` under `android/**/res/` fails the whole Android build
# with `Resource and asset merger: The file name must end with .xml or .png` — an error that names the
# file but not the reason it is there. Fifty-three appeared in one sync pass.
#
# There is no AGP-level ignore for this: `androidResources.ignoreAssetsPatterns` is applied by aapt2,
# which the merge task runs before, and `sourceSets["main"].res.exclude` does not reach the merger
# either. Both were tried. So `tools/check_workspace.py` reports them, and the fix is to delete them.
desktop.ini
.kotlin/

# Folder metadata written by cloud-sync clients — Google Drive Desktop in this case, which puts one in
# every folder it manages (the content names `GoogleDriveFS.exe`). `OneDrive litter` was this line's
# earlier description and named the wrong program.
#
# **Ignoring them here is not enough, and that is the trap.** Gradle's resource merger scans the
# filesystem rather than git, so a `desktop.ini` under `android/**/res/` fails the whole Android build
# with `Resource and asset merger: The file name must end with .xml or .png` — an error that names the
# file but not the reason it is there. Fifty-three appeared in one sync pass.
#
# There is no AGP-level ignore for this: `androidResources.ignoreAssetsPatterns` is applied by aapt2,
# which the merge task runs before, and `sourceSets["main"].res.exclude` does not reach the merger
# either. Both were tried. So `tools/check_workspace.py` reports them, and the fix is to delete them.
desktop.ini
.kotlin/

# A checkout of the rchify skill that landed in the working tree during an unrelated probe. It is
# not a build input, not referenced anywhere in this repository, and not something to commit — but it is
# 1.3 MB of vendored code, so it is named here rather than left to show up in git status for ever.
.archify-probe/

# Android signing key material for ssembleRelease. **Never commit these**: a signing key in a public
# repository is a signing key everyone has, and Android refuses an in-place update signed by a
# different one. Absent both, the release build is unsigned, which is the published artifact today.
keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
